#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:632
#: 71a59a18a40c42c984657fbe51bcacd8
msgid "This section lists the analog pins available on the Pixhawk. These are virtual pins, defined in the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:635
#: 00aec41e4f4643d8b41b4db129e0e760
msgid "**Virtual Pin 2 and Power connector Pin 4**: power management connector voltage pin, accepts up to 3.3V, usually attached to a power module with 10.1:1 scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:639
#: 3402dcd761f941b0b2b9bf1cc77b81d7
msgid "**Virtual Pin 3 and Power connector Pin 3**: power management connector current pin, accepts up to 3.3V, usually attached to a power module with 17:1 scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:643
#: 25dd44b3e7fd43f8b480595727e03fe3
msgid "**Virtual Pin 4 and (No connector Pin)**: VCC 5V rail sensing. This virtual pin reads the voltage on the 5V supply rail. It is used to provide the HWSTATUS.Vcc reading that ground stations use to display 5V status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:648
#: 666061616698421c85c07cb0bf3497ee
msgid "**Virtual Pin 13 and ADC 3.3V connector Pin 4**: This takes a max of 3.3V. May be used for sonar or other analog sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:651
#: 71dde1d121364954846d87d9418a6593
msgid "**Virtual Pin 14 and ADC 3.3V connector Pin 2**: This takes a max of 3.3V. May be used for second sonar or other analog sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:654
#: 339b04e7f3574ff8a5d4af533090703d
msgid "**Virtual Pin 15 and ADC 6.6V connector Pin 2**: analog airspeed sensor port. This has 2:1 scaling builtin, so can take up to 6.6v analog inputs. Usually used for analog airspeed, but may be used for analog sonar or other analog sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:662
#: 91ef8dd4f35f4588807c575c552fc13f
msgid "**Virtual Pin 102**: Servo power rail voltage. This is an internal measurement of the servo rail voltage made by the IO board within the Pixhawk. It has 3:1 scaling, allowing it to measure up to 9.9V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:666
#: 9317a62c914045eaad1f2cc93dd0d509
msgid "**Virtual Pin 103**: RSSI (Received Signal Strength Input) input pin voltage (SBus connector output pin). This is the voltage measured by the RSSI input pin on the SBUS-out connector (the bottom pin of the 2nd last servo connector on the 14 connector servo rail)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:671
#: 641058e6a3d343d3931bf90c7ed5afc1
msgid "This can alternatively serve as SBus out by setting the ``BRD_SBUS_OUT`` parameter ( :ref:`Copter <copter:BRD_SBUS_OUT>`, :ref:`Plane <plane:BRD_SBUS_OUT>`, :ref:`Rover <rover:BRD_SBUS_OUT>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:681
#: fd6f53066fa84a3e818178ad4086547c
msgid "Pixhawk digital outputs and inputs (Virtual Pins 50-55)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:683
#: cd2576d90e6842fc8e38fc7ff8df1a05
msgid "The Pixhawk has no dedicated digital output or input pins on its DF13 connectors, but you can assign up to 6 of the \"AUX SERVO\" connectors to be digital GPIO outputs/inputs. These are the first 6 of the 14 three-pin servo connectors on the end of the board. They are marked as AUX servo pins 1 - 6 on the silkscreen as seen above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:689
#: 21520e37457f41dc9cd956411b20e886
msgid "To set the number of these pins that are available as digital inputs/outputs, set the ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` parameter. On Pixhawk this defaults to 4, which means the first 4 AUX connectors are for servos (PWM) and the last 2 are for digital inputs/outputs. If you set ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` to 0 then you would have 6 virtual digital pins and still have 8 PWM outputs on the rest of the connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:696
#: 8c1063d9b37046468c496a8b1a3c9cf0
msgid "in firmware versions 4.2 and later, the method for setting a PWM/SERVO/MOTOR output to be a GPIO function is changed. Instead of ``BRD_PWM_COUNT`` being used, the individual ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameter is merely set to \"-1\". If set to \"0\", it remains a PWM output, unassigned to a function, and outputs that output's trim value when board safety is not active. If the servo function is being \"mirrored\" to a remote device, as in the case of a DroneCAN or KDECAN ESC, then in order to change the autopilot board's corresponding output pin to be a GPIO, but allow the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` to still be assigned to the remote device, the :ref:`SERVO_GPIO_MASK<SERVO_GPIO_MASK>` parameter can be used to assign the board pin to be a GPIO without affecting the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` assignment for the remote device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-pixhawk-overview.rst:698
#: 2123a91f44a8487ba4b105db854a974a
msgid "The 6 possible pins are available for PIN variables as pin numbers 50 to 55 inclusive."
msgstr ""

